      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,1)$,$(2,2)$,$(3,-1)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,1)}=1\\frac{(1)^{2}}{(-2)}=- \\frac{1}{2}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,2)}=1\\frac{(2)^{2}}{(2)}=2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(3,-1)}=1\\frac{(-1)^{2}}{(3)}=\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/repairs/2026-10-20-early-cohort/jobs/17592186172038/review-3-policy-2-b6fc68f59ef8c5ba/assets/a92c9aa24250a2f67d768b9aef11463d62665d7fa17fd7124de870ffd2f6a9f1.png)",
